1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,340
Quentin Tarantino, one of the most acclaimed filmmakers of all time, known for bringing his bold ideas to life with surreal visuals and mind-bending storytelling.

2
00:00:08,340 --> 00:00:17,040
But he wasn't always a Hollywood icon. Once he was just an ordinary guy working at a video store. Until one night, he decided to rewrite his story.

3
00:00:17,040 --> 00:00:29,680
And there was like one night, I'd stay up all night long and rather than give myself excuses, I would look at everything that I'm in my life or everything I'm not doing or whatever and just not give myself any excuses out.

4
00:00:29,680 --> 00:00:31,680
Just like nail it.

5
00:00:31,680 --> 00:00:35,680
And I would spend like all night laying out everything I'm doing that's wrong.

6
00:00:35,680 --> 00:00:38,680
And then I would spend the last two hours figuring out how I can change it.

7
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:42,680
And as opposed to just doing it and then going to get some sleep.

8
00:00:42,680 --> 00:00:43,680
I decided to change my life.

9
00:00:43,680 --> 00:00:48,680
Today I present you the Tarantino method. To follow this process, you'll need three things.

10
00:00:48,680 --> 00:00:53,680
A pen, a notepad, and the dead of night. When the world is silent and not a soul is awake.

11
00:00:53,680 --> 00:00:55,680
That's when it can happen. Trust.

12
00:00:55,680 --> 00:00:58,680
Now it begins. The first page is always going to be the hardest,

13
00:00:58,680 --> 00:01:08,240
Now that you've started, you have to ask yourself the big, scary, fear mongering question.

14
00:01:08,240 --> 00:01:24,187
What am I doing wrong Be brutally honest As Quinton himself would say Nail it Take your time Dive deep It gritty It tough but it absolutely necessary And when you push through boom you halfway there

15
00:01:24,187 --> 00:01:37,787
It's all out there. The fears, the doubts, the mistakes, the lessons, the heartbreak, all laid out, bare for you to see. Not built up in your mind, but on paper, tangible.

16
00:01:37,787 --> 00:01:43,787
Take a moment, because now you have to ask yourself, how can I change it?

17
00:01:43,787 --> 00:01:48,287
We're not all Quentin Tarantino. You might be feeling like you're all written out.

18
00:01:48,287 --> 00:01:51,787
So let's make this part simple. A straightforward list.

19
00:01:51,787 --> 00:01:55,787
100 ways you can change your life. Quite a simple process.

20
00:01:55,787 --> 00:01:59,287
Take a mistake you've learned and write down a way to change it.

21
00:01:59,287 --> 00:02:03,787
Repeat it over and over again. Push forward. Write it down.

22
00:02:03,787 --> 00:02:06,787
Adapt, reflect, learn, and grow.

23
00:02:06,787 --> 00:02:09,087
Until finally, when you ask yourself,

24
00:02:09,087 --> 00:02:10,487
how can I change my life?

25
00:02:10,487 --> 00:02:11,987
You'll have a hundred ways to do it.

26
00:02:11,987 --> 00:02:13,587
But there's one very important thing

27
00:02:13,587 --> 00:02:15,587
you need to remember throughout this whole night.

28
00:02:15,587 --> 00:02:17,587
You gotta actually f***ing do it.
